# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Without this, Git applies `core.autocrlf` on Windows and rewrites every text file
# to CRLF in the working tree, so a diff can show a whole file as changed when only
# one line moved. The plugin ships shell-runnable scripts and a YAML patch document,
# and both are read by tools that do not want CRLF, so the repository stores LF and
# the checkout keeps LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touch their line endings or try to diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.bmp binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts, where CRLF is the convention the interpreter expects.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
